          "AccrualMethod" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Defines how leave credits are granted to workers. Allowed values: \"AWARDED\", \"ACCRUED\".\n\n- AWARDED: Balance is granted immediately upon assignment (no scheduling required).\n- ACCRUED: Balance accumulates periodically on a defined schedule (requires scheduler creation).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`service/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n- When AccrualMethod == \"ACCRUED\", ValidateAccrualSchedule is called to validate cycle parameters and generate a schedulerName. A scheduler is then created via CreateAccrualScheduler.\n- When AccrualMethod == \"AWARDED\", no scheduler is created.\n- AccrualRate, AccrualCycleDay, AccrualCycleMonth, AccrualFrequency, and AccrualRateUnit are all validated as dependent attributes that require AccrualMethod == \"ACCRUED\" to be meaningful.\n  Validation expression: accrual.AccrualMethod == null ? null : (accrual.AccrualMethod == 'ACCRUED' ? 'true' : 'false')\n\n[`service/accrual/UpdateAccrual.gloop`]\n- If AccrualMethod is changed from AWARDED → ACCRUED: a new scheduler is created.\n- If AccrualMethod is changed from ACCRUED → AWARDED: the existing scheduler is deleted.\n- The same dependent-attribute validation as InsertAccrual is applied on update.\n\n**Example:** `ACCRUED`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
