            "description" : "The amount of leave credited to a worker per accrual cycle, expressed in the unit defined by AccrualRateUnit. Only meaningful when AccrualMethod == \"ACCRUED\".\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`service/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n[`service/accrual/UpdateAccrual.gloop`]\n- Validated as a dependent attribute of AccrualMethod: required when AccrualMethod is \"ACCRUED\", and must be null when not applicable.\n\n[`sql/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n[`sql/accrual/UpdateAccrual.gloop`]\n- Persisted as a DECIMAL column. On update, uses COALESCE.\n\n[`service/accrual/GenerateAccrualBalance.gloop`]\n- Applied directly to the worker's AccrualBalance during scheduled accrual processing:\n    - AccruedAmount += AccrualRate\n    - Balance += AccrualRate\n- Before applying, the system checks that AccruedAmount + AccrualRate does not exceed MaxAnnualAccrual. If it would, the update is skipped for that cycle.\n\n**Example:** `3.08`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
