          "AccrualCycleDay" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Day component of the accrual processing schedule. Allowed values: \"1\"–\"31\" or \"*\" (wildcard). Only meaningful when AccrualMethod == \"ACCRUED\".\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`service/accrual/ValidateAccrualSchedule.gloop`]\n- ANNUALLY: Must be a specific number (not \"*\"). Combined with AccrualCycleMonth to produce a valid calendar date. Scheduler name: \"YearlyMonth{M}Day{D}AccrualScheduler\".\n- MONTHLY: Must be a specific number (not \"\\*\"). AccrualCycleMonth is automatically overridden to \"*\". Scheduler name: \"MonthlyDay{D}AccrualScheduler\".\n- DAILY: Automatically set to \"*\" regardless of input. Scheduler name: \"DailyAccrualScheduler\".\n\n[`service/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n[`service/accrual/UpdateAccrual.gloop`]\n- Validated as a dependent attribute of AccrualMethod.\n- The validated/corrected value returned by ValidateAccrualSchedule is written back to the accrual model before the SQL insert/update.\n\n[`service/accrual/GenerateAccrualBalance.gloop`]\n- Used by SelectAllAccrualByAccrualCycle to match schedulers to their target accrual policies when the scheduler fires. The scheduler passes its \"days\" property, which is matched against this field.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
