          "CanCarryForward" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Boolean flag indicating whether a worker's remaining accrual balance at fiscal year-end is carried over into the new fiscal year. When false, the balance resets to zero.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`sql/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n[`sql/accrual/UpdateAccrual.gloop`]\n- Stored in the database as an integer (1 = true, 0 = false, null = null).\n  Insert expression: accrual.CanCarryForward == null ? null : (accrual.CanCarryForward ? 1 : 0)\n  On update, uses COALESCE.\n\n[`service/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n[`service/accrual/UpdateAccrual.gloop`]\n- Validated as a dependency of CarryForwardLimit: when CanCarryForward is true, CarryForwardLimit is required.\n\n[`service/accrual/ProcessFiscalYearEndAccrualBalance.gloop`]\n- Checked at fiscal year-end as the branching condition for carry-forward processing.\n    NOTE: Compared using the integer value \"1\" (not the boolean true) due to legacy integer storage in the database.\n    - If CanCarryForward == 1: CarryOver = min(Balance, CarryForwardLimit); new Balance = CarryOver; AccruedAmount reset to 0.\n    - If CanCarryForward == 0 (or null): Balance and AccruedAmount are both reset to 0; CarryOver = 0.\n\n**Example:** `true`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
