            "description" : "The maximum number of leave units that can be carried over into the next fiscal year. Only meaningful when CanCarryForward == true.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`service/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n[`service/accrual/UpdateAccrual.gloop`]\n- Validated as a dependent attribute of CanCarryForward: required when CanCarryForward is true, should be null when CanCarryForward is false.\n\n[`sql/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n[`sql/accrual/UpdateAccrual.gloop`]\n- Persisted as a DECIMAL column. On update, uses COALESCE.\n\n[`service/accrual/ProcessFiscalYearEndAccrualBalance.gloop`]\n- Used as the cap in the carry-forward calculation at fiscal year-end:\n  CarryOver = min(Balance, CarryForwardLimit)\n  The lower of the actual balance or this limit is carried forward.\n\n**Example:** `80.00`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team\n**Version:** 1.0\n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
