          "WaitingDays" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Number of days after a worker's employment start date before they become eligible to accrue leave under this policy. Acts as a probationary period gate.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`service/accrual/GenerateAccrualBalance.gloop`]\n- During each scheduled accrual run, if WaitingDays is set:\n  1. The worker's EmploymentStartDate is fetched.\n  2. WaitingDays is added to EmploymentStartDate to compute WorkerAccrualStartDate.\n  3. If the current date < WorkerAccrualStartDate, the balance update is skipped for that worker.\n- This means newly hired workers do not receive accruals until their waiting period has elapsed.\n\n[`sql/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n[`sql/accrual/UpdateAccrual.gloop`]\n- Persisted as an integer column. On update, uses COALESCE.\n\n**Example:** `90`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team\n**Version:** 1.0\n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
