          "AllowEncashment" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Boolean flag on the accrual policy that controls whether workers are permitted to convert their accrual balance into monetary compensation.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`service/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n- Stored in the database as an integer (1 = true, 0 = false, null = null).\n  Expression: accrual.AllowEncashment == null ? null : (accrual.AllowEncashment ? 1 : 0)\n- Accepted as part of the accrual input model when creating a new accrual policy.\n\n[`service/accrual_balance/InsertAccrualBalance.gloop`]\n[`service/accrual_balance/UpdateAccrualBalance.gloop`]\n- When AllowEncashment is true, the EarningId field on the accrual balance is REQUIRED.\n  If missing, the insert/update is rejected with: \"EarningId must be provided for cashable accruals.\"\n- When AllowEncashment is false, the EarningId field on the accrual balance must be NULL.\n  If provided, the insert/update is rejected with: \"EarningId must be null for non-cashable accruals.\"\n\n[`service/payroll_run/ProcessAccrualBalances.gloop`]\n- Checked at payroll run time as the second gate (after the global encashAccrualBalances flag).\n  Full condition: encashAccrualBalances == true AND AllowEncashment == true AND AccrualBalance.Earning.Id != null\n- Only when all three conditions are met does the system calculate the encashable amount and add it to the worker's gross pay.\n- The encashable balance is computed using the linked Earning's CalculationMethod (FLAT or PERCENT) and is clamped by PayPeriodMin/PayPeriodMax.\n- The encashed amount is multiplied by the worker's OriginalBaseRate to produce the monetary EmployeeAmount.\n- The accrual balance is then reduced by the encashed amount (Balance -= EncashableBalance, Used += EncashableBalance).\n\n[`service/payroll_run/SelectAllPayComponentByWorkerAndPosition.gloop`]\n- AllowEncashment is loaded from the ACCRUAL table (via SelectAccrual) onto the Accrual sub-model of each AccrualBalance entry during payroll data assembly, making it available downstream to ProcessAccrualBalances.\n\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
