          },
          "CompanyId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Foreign key linking this accrual policy to its owning company. Used to scope all queries and processing operations to the correct company.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`sql/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n- Inserted as a non-null integer column into the ACCRUAL table.\n\n[`service/accrual/GenerateAccrualBalance.gloop`]\n- Used to fetch the Company record (via SelectCompany) in order to compute CompanyFiscalYearStart and CompanyFiscalYearEnd, which gate whether a scheduled accrual update should proceed.\n\n[`service/accrual/ProcessFiscalYearEndAccrualBalance.gloop`]\n- Accrual policies are discovered per company (SelectAllAccrualByCompany) using CompanyId so that fiscal year-end processing is fully company-scoped.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CreatedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp of when the accrual policy record was first inserted into the database. Set automatically to the current datetime on creation and never updated afterwards.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`service/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n- Set to \"now\" at insert time via the expression: now\n\n[`sql/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n- Mapped to the CreatedDate column in the INSERT statement. Not included in the UpdateAccrual SQL.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-15 08:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CreatedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who created the accrual policy record. Populated from the UserId input at creation time and never updated afterwards.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`service/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n- Mapped from the UserId input parameter: insertAccrualInput.CreatedBy = UserId\n\n[`sql/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n- Persisted in the CreatedBy column on INSERT. Not included in the UpdateAccrual SQL.\n\n**Example:** `admin`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "UpdatedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp of the most recent modification to the accrual policy record. Set to the current datetime on both creation and every subsequent update.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`service/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n- Set to \"now\" at insert time (same as CreatedDate).\n\n[`service/accrual/UpdateAccrual.gloop`]\n- Set to \"now\" on every update: updateAccrualInput.UpdatedDate = now\n\n[`sql/accrual/UpdateAccrual.gloop`]\n- Included in the UPDATE statement. Uses COALESCE.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-15 08:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "UpdatedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who last modified the accrual policy record. Set to UserId on creation and refreshed on every update.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`service/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n- Mapped from the UserId input parameter at creation: insertAccrualInput.UpdatedBy = UserId\n\n[`service/accrual/UpdateAccrual.gloop`]\n- Refreshed on every update: updateAccrualInput.UpdatedBy = UserId\n\n[`sql/accrual/UpdateAccrual.gloop`]\n- Included in the UPDATE statement. Uses COALESCE.\n\n**Example:** `admin`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "DeletedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp of when the accrual policy was soft-deleted. Null when the record is active. Part of the soft-delete pattern used across the payroll application.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`sql/accrual/DeleteAccrual.gloop`]\n- Set during soft-delete alongside DeletedBy and Deleted = 1. The record is not physically removed from the database.\n\n**Example:** `null`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "DeletedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who soft-deleted the accrual policy record.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`sql/accrual/DeleteAccrual.gloop`]\n- Set during soft-delete alongside DeletedDate and Deleted = 1.\n\n**Example:** `null`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Deleted" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Boolean soft-delete flag. When true, the record is considered logically deleted and is excluded from all active queries.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`sql/accrual/InsertAccrual.gloop`]\n- Not set on INSERT; defaults to false (0) in the database.\n\n[`sql/accrual/DeleteAccrual.gloop`]\n- Set to 1 (true) during soft-delete, along with DeletedDate and DeletedBy.\n  The DELETE operation in this codebase is implemented as an UPDATE, not a physical row removal.\n\n[`sql/accrual/SelectAccrual.gloop`]\n[`sql/accrual/SelectAllAccrual.gloop`]\n- All SELECT queries filter on Deleted = 0 (or equivalent) so that soft-deleted policies are never returned in normal operations.\n\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 10, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          }
        },
        "additionalProperties" : false
      },
