      "lonti_app_payroll_model_Earning" : {
        "properties" : {
          "Id" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Unique auto-generated primary key for the earning record.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Populated from the database-generated key after a successful INSERT (`$getGeneratedKeys` flag set to true): `$gloopOutput.generatedKeys.Id`.\n- Confirmed alongside `updateCount > 0` before returning the API response and logging to the tracker.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/DeleteEarning.gloop`]\n- Used as the lookup key in a SELECT-before-mutate check; a null result from `SelectEarning` produces a 404 \"record not found\" response before any DML is executed.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/ValidateEarning.gloop`]\n- Passed as `EarningId` to `SelectEarning`; a null result throws an exception re-raised as 404, blocking any service that requires a valid earning reference.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/DeleteEarning.gloop`]\n- Passed to `SelectPositionPayComponentCountByEarning` and `SelectWorkerPayComponentCountByEarning` to validate that no downstream assignment records reference this earning before soft-deletion proceeds.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/earning/DeleteEarning.gloop`]\n- Used within the soft-delete SQL `CONCAT` expressions to generate placeholder strings for anonymized fields (e.g., `'Deleted Earning {Id} Name'`).\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Name" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Human-readable display name for the earning (e.g., \"Regular Pay\", \"Overtime\", \"Annual Leave\").\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Required on creation; `ValidateRequiredFields` enforces that `Name` is not null.\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful INSERT.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional on update; updated via `COALESCE(:Name, \"Name\")`.\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful UPDATE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/DeleteEarning.gloop`]\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful DELETE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/earning/DeleteEarning.gloop`]\n- Overwritten directly in the database during soft-delete with the placeholder string `'Deleted Earning {Id} Name'`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n- Surfaced on `EarningLogs` entries in the PaySlip preview for display (appended with `\" (tax-exempt)\"` when the earning falls below the tax exemption threshold).\n\n**Example:** `Regular Pay`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Type" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Tax timing classification for the earning. Allowed values: `PRETAX`, `POSTTAX`.\n\nNOTE: The applicability of `PRETAX`/`POSTTAX` logic to earnings is under review. Current internal usage primarily applies this classification to benefit deductions. Industry standards review is identified as needed to determine whether this field should be retained, removed, or restructured for earnings specifically.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Required on creation; `ValidateRequiredFields` enforces that `Type` is not null.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n- Branched on alongside `IsTaxable` to route the calculated amount into `GrossTaxable`/`GrossNonTaxable`/`NetTaxable` when `Type = PRETAX`. The `POSTTAX` branch applies a simpler non-taxable route when `IsTaxable = false`.\n\n**Example:** `PRETAX`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true,
            "enum" : [ "PRETAX", "POSTTAX" ]
          },
          "Code" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Short identifier code for the earning. For accrual-linked earnings, this is auto-populated from the linked `Accrual.Code` and cannot be manually specified. For non-accrual earnings, it must be explicitly provided.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Governed by the four-scenario Accrual-Code rule (see top-level model comment for full detail):\n    - `AccrualId` provided, `Code` null → auto-set from `Accrual.Code` via `ValidateAccrual`.\n    - `AccrualId` provided, `Code` also provided → 400 error.\n    - `AccrualId` null, `Code` provided → accepted as-is.\n    - `AccrualId` null, `Code` null → 400 error.\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful INSERT.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional on update; updated via `COALESCE`.\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful UPDATE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/DeleteEarning.gloop`]\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful DELETE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/earning/DeleteEarning.gloop`]\n- Overwritten in the database during soft-delete with the placeholder string `'Deleted Earning {Id} Code'`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n- Surfaced on `EarningLogs` entries in the PaySlip preview for display.\n\n**Example:** `REG`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Description" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Optional free-text description providing additional context about the earning.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional on creation; not included in `ValidateRequiredFields`.\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful INSERT.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional on update; updated via `COALESCE`.\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful UPDATE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/DeleteEarning.gloop`]\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful DELETE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/earning/DeleteEarning.gloop`]\n- Overwritten in the database during soft-delete with the placeholder string `'Deleted Earning {Id} Description'`.\n\n**Example:** `Standard regular pay earning component.`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Active" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Boolean flag indicating whether the earning is currently active. Stored as an integer in the database (1 = true, 0 = false).\n\nNOTE: This property is currently informational only (PAYROLL-159). Payroll processing does not filter earnings by `Active` status. Implementation to make this field functional is planned and will be prioritized for the Worker entity to enable payroll exclusion.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Required on creation; `ValidateRequiredFields` enforces that `Active` is not null.\n- Converted to integer before INSERT: `earning.Active == null ? null : (earning.Active ? 1 : 0)`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional on update; converted to integer and updated via `COALESCE`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/earning/DeleteEarning.gloop`]\n- Explicitly set to `0` (false) by the soft-delete SQL, in addition to setting `Deleted = 1`.\n\n**Example:** `true`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "EffectiveFromDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The date from which this earning takes effect, defining the start of its active window.\n\nNOTE: This property is currently informational only. Payroll processing does not filter or gate earnings based on effective dates.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Required on creation; `ValidateRequiredFields` enforces that `EffectiveFromDate` is not null.\n- Validated for date string format via `ValidateDates` (format-only on insert, no range check).\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional on update; when provided, validated for both format and date range via `ValidateDates`.\n- Updated via `COALESCE`; preserved on soft-delete.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-15 00:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "EffectiveToDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Optional end date defining when this earning expires. Null indicates no expiry.\n\nNOTE: This property is currently informational only. Payroll processing does not filter or gate earnings based on effective dates.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional on creation; validated for date string format via `ValidateDates` when provided.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional on update; when provided, validated for both format and date range via `ValidateDates`.\n- Updated via `COALESCE`; preserved on soft-delete.\n\n**Example:** `2099-12-31 00:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Frequency" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Informational label indicating how often this earning is processed (e.g., \"MONTHLY\", \"BIWEEKLY\"). Originally intended to allow individual earnings to fire at a different frequency than the pay schedule.\n\nNOTE: This property is currently not consumed by any payroll processing logic. The feature to support earnings at a different frequency than the pay schedule was planned but not implemented in the initial system. No ticket currently exists for its implementation.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional; persisted on INSERT and updated via `COALESCE` on UPDATE. No validation applied beyond storage.\n- Preserved on soft-delete (commented out in SQL).\n\n**Example:** `MONTHLY`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "NeedAttendance" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Boolean flag indicating whether this earning requires a corresponding `Attendance_Summary` record for the worker and pay period before it can be processed. Stored as an integer in the database (1 = true, 0 = false).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Required on creation; `ValidateRequiredFields` enforces that `NeedAttendance` is not null.\n- Converted to integer before INSERT: `earning.NeedAttendance == null ? null : (earning.NeedAttendance ? 1 : 0)`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n- Branched on during payroll processing. When `NeedAttendance = true`, the earning calculation uses attendance units (`Units` and `UnitsType` from the linked `Attendance_Summary` record) rather than a fixed amount.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/ValidateAttendanceSummaryDetails.gloop`]\n- Checked when importing attendance CSV records: if the resolved earning has `NeedAttendance = false`, the error `'Earning record does not need Attendance Summary records.'` is returned and the attendance record is rejected.\n\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CalculationMethodId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Foreign key referencing the primary `CalculationMethod` record that defines how this earning's base amount is computed (`FLAT` or `PERCENT` of the position's pay period rate).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Required on creation; `ValidateRequiredFields` enforces that `CalculationMethodId` is not null.\n- Validated via `ValidateCalculationMethod` to confirm the referenced record exists.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional on update; when supplied, validated via `ValidateCalculationMethod`. Updated via `COALESCE`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n- Resolved at payroll run time via `SelectCalculationMethod`. When `Method = PERCENT`, `Amount` is multiplied by the position's `PayPeriodRate`; when `Method = FLAT`, `Amount` is used directly. The `Amount` may also be scaled by attendance `Units` when `NeedAttendance = true`.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Units" : {
            "type" : "number",
            "description" : "The quantity of units associated with this earning.\n\nNOTE: This property is not supplied through the CRUD services (`InsertEarning`, `UpdateEarning`); it is not present in the SQL INSERT or UPDATE statements. It exists in the `SelectEarning` output model and is carried through the payroll assembly pipeline but is not used.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/SelectAllPayComponentByWorkerAndPosition.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/SelectAllEarningAndBenefitByWorkerAndPosition.gloop`]\n- Hydrated from `SelectEarning` into the earning sub-model during payroll assembly.\n\n**Example:** `1.00`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "double",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "UnitsType" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The unit of measurement for `Units`. Allowed values: `DAY`, `HOUR`, `UNIT`.\n\nNOTE: Like `Units`, this property is not managed through the CRUD services. It exists in the `SelectEarning` output and is carried through the payroll assembly pipeline but is not used.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/SelectAllPayComponentByWorkerAndPosition.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/SelectAllEarningAndBenefitByWorkerAndPosition.gloop`]\n- Hydrated from `SelectEarning` into the earning sub-model during payroll assembly.\n\n**Example:** `HOUR`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true,
            "enum" : [ "DAY", "HOUR", "UNIT" ]
          },
          "Amount" : {
            "type" : "number",
            "description" : "The base earning amount, interpreted according to `CalculationMethodId`: a flat monetary value for `FLAT`, or a multiplier applied to the position's `PayPeriodRate` for `PERCENT`.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Required on creation; `ValidateRequiredFields` enforces that `Amount` is not null.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional on update; updated via `COALESCE`; preserved on soft-delete.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n- At payroll run time, the effective amount is resolved as `CustomAmount ?: Amount` (worker-level override takes precedence via `Worker_Pay_Component`).\n- When `CalculationMethod.Method = PERCENT`, the effective amount is multiplied by the position's `PayPeriodRate`.\n- When `NeedAttendance = true`, the amount is further scaled by attendance units.\n- The final amount is clamped between `PayPeriodMin` and `PayPeriodMax` via `ClampAmount` before being applied to the payslip.\n\n**Example:** `0.00`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "double",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "ShiftDifferential" : {
            "type" : "number",
            "description" : "An additional amount applied on top of the base earning amount to compensate for non-standard shift work. When non-null, `SDCalculationMethodId` is required. Interpreted as a multiplier for `PERCENT` (`EmployeeAmount × ShiftDifferential`) or a flat additive for `FLAT` (`EmployeeAmount + ShiftDifferential`).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional; when non-null (and non-zero), acts as the parent dependency in `ValidateDependentAttributes`, requiring `SDCalculationMethodId` to also be provided. The dependency value is evaluated as `(earning.ShiftDifferential) ? 'not null' : null`, meaning a zero value is treated as null/absent and does not trigger the requirement. Technical debt ticket: PAYROLL-261.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional on update; updated via `COALESCE`. Validated against existing values via dual-state `ValidateDependentAttributes`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n- Checked as non-null gate: if `ShiftDifferential != null`, the shift differential is applied after base calculation.\n- `PERCENT` method: `EmployeeAmount += EmployeeAmount × ShiftDifferential`.\n- `FLAT` method: `EmployeeAmount += ShiftDifferential`.\n\n**Example:** `0.00`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "double",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "SDCalculationMethodId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Foreign key referencing the `CalculationMethod` record that defines how the shift differential is applied. Required when `ShiftDifferential` is non-null and non-zero.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Conditionally required: enforced by `ValidateDependentAttributes` when `ShiftDifferential` is non-null/non-zero.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional on update; updated via `COALESCE`. Validated as part of the `ShiftDifferential` dependent attribute check.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n- Resolved at payroll run time via `SelectCalculationMethod` when shift differential processing is triggered. Determines whether the differential is applied as `PERCENT` (multiplicative) or `FLAT` (additive).\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "IsTaxable" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Boolean flag indicating whether this earning is subject to income tax. Stored as an integer in the database (1 = true, 0 = false).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Required on creation; `ValidateRequiredFields` enforces that `IsTaxable` is not null.\n- Converted to integer before INSERT: `earning.IsTaxable == null ? null : (earning.IsTaxable ? 1 : 0)`.\n- Acts as the parent dependency in `ValidateDependentAttributes`: when true, `TaxExemptionAmount` is required on insert.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional on update; converted to integer and updated via `COALESCE`. Validated against existing values via dual-state `ValidateDependentAttributes`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n- For `Type = PRETAX` earnings: when `IsTaxable = true`, the amount is split between `GrossTaxable` (above `TaxExemptionAmount`) and `GrossNonTaxable` (at or below it). When `IsTaxable = false`, the full amount goes to `GrossNonTaxable`.\n- Preserved on soft-delete (commented out in SQL).\n\n**Example:** `true`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "TaxExemptionAmount" : {
            "type" : "number",
            "description" : "The portion of the earning amount that is exempt from income tax. Required when `IsTaxable = true` on insert.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Required when `IsTaxable = true`: `ValidateDependentAttributes` is invoked with no `CurrentDependents` (insert mode), applying the insert branch — a null `TaxExemptionAmount` throws a 400 error when `IsTaxable = true`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional on update; validated against existing values via dual-state `ValidateDependentAttributes`. A null new value is permitted on update if an existing value is already stored.\n- Updated via `COALESCE`; preserved on soft-delete.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n- For `Type = PRETAX, IsTaxable = true` earnings:\n    - If `EmployeeAmount <= TaxExemptionAmount`: full amount is non-taxable (`GrossNonTaxable`).\n    - If `EmployeeAmount > TaxExemptionAmount`: excess goes to `GrossTaxable` + `NetTaxable`; exempt portion goes to `GrossNonTaxable`. Both portions are logged to `EarningLogs`.\n\n**Example:** `0.00`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "double",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "TaxCalculationMethodId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Foreign key referencing the `CalculationMethod` used for tax calculation on this earning. Exists in the database schema and is returned by `SelectEarning`, but is not currently populated or validated by the service layer.\n\nNOTE: This property is not actively used. The `InsertEarning` and `UpdateEarning` service files never map a value to this field, so it is always persisted as null through the service layer. It is reserved for future tax calculation method integration.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/earning/SelectEarning.gloop`]\n- Returned as part of the SELECT output.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "PayPeriodMax" : {
            "type" : "number",
            "description" : "The maximum amount that may be applied for this earning in a single pay period. Acts as an upper clamp on the calculated earning amount during payroll processing.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional; persisted on INSERT and updated via `COALESCE` on UPDATE. Preserved on soft-delete.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n- Passed as `maxLimit` to `ClampAmount` after the base earning amount (plus any shift differential) is calculated. If the calculated amount exceeds this value, it is capped at `PayPeriodMax`.\n\n**Example:** `0.00`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "double",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "PayPeriodMin" : {
            "type" : "number",
            "description" : "The minimum amount that must be applied for this earning in a single pay period. Acts as a lower clamp on the calculated earning amount during payroll processing.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional; persisted on INSERT and updated via `COALESCE` on UPDATE. Preserved on soft-delete.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n- Passed as `minLimit` to `ClampAmount` after the base earning amount is calculated. If the calculated amount falls below this value, it is raised to `PayPeriodMin`.\n\n**Example:** `0.00`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "double",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "AccrualId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Optional foreign key referencing the `Accrual` policy that this earning is linked to for leave-consumption tracking. When set, attendance summaries imported against this earning will look up the worker's `AccrualBalance` for that accrual and update it — decrementing `Balance` and incrementing `Used` by the units worked. This earning is therefore the **leave-consumption earning**: it tracks the actual use of leave credits through attendance records.\n\nThis is distinct from the **encashment earning**, which is a separate earning record stored on `AccrualBalance.EarningId`. The encashment earning is used during payroll runs to pay out accrual balances in cash, and does not involve attendance records.\n\nWhen `AccrualId` is provided, `Code` must be null — it is auto-populated from `Accrual.Code`. See the top-level model comment for the full four-scenario rule.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- When non-null and `Code` is null: `ValidateAccrual` is called to confirm the accrual exists, and `earning.Code` is set to `selectAccrualOutput.Code`.\n- When non-null and `Code` is also provided: returns 400 \"Code will be set to the Accrual's Code if AccrualId is provided.\"\n- When null: normal earning path; `Code` must be explicitly supplied.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/ValidateAttendanceSummaryDetails.gloop`]\n- When an earning has a non-null `AccrualId`, the attendance import calls `SelectAccrualBalanceByAccrualAndWorker` using `earning.AccrualId` and the worker's Id to locate the worker's `AccrualBalance`. If no balance record is found, the error `'Worker does not have a credit record for Leave.'` is returned. If found, the balance is validated for sufficient credits (unless `allowNegativeBalance = true`) and the updated `Balance` and `Used` values are prepared for persistence alongside the attendance record.\n\n**Example:** `null`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CompanyId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Foreign key scoping this earning to a specific company. Ensures earnings are company-specific and cannot be shared across companies.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Required on creation; `ValidateRequiredFields` enforces that `CompanyId` is not null.\n- Validated via `ValidateCompany` to confirm the referenced company exists.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Present in the UPDATE SQL via `COALESCE`; the service layer does not supply it on update, making it effectively immutable post-creation.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/ValidateAttendanceSummaryDetails.gloop`]\n- The resolved earning's `CompanyId` is compared against the pay period's company to enforce company consistency: `PayPeriodCompanyId != earning.CompanyId` → returns 400 \"Earning is not owned by the Company the selected Pay Period is under.\"\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CurrencyId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Optional foreign key referencing the `Currency` record that denominates this earning's amounts.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Optional; persisted on INSERT and updated via `COALESCE` on UPDATE. No validation against the `Currency` table is applied at the service layer.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/SelectAllPayComponentByWorkerAndPosition.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/SelectAllEarningAndBenefitByWorkerAndPosition.gloop`]\n- Hydrated into the currency sub-model (`CurrencyName`, `CurrencySymbol`, `IsoCurrencyCode`, `CurrencyPrecision`) via `SelectCurrency` during payroll assembly; surfaced on `EarningLogs` entries for display.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CreatedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp recording when the earning record was first inserted into the database.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Set to the current server timestamp (`now`) by the service layer before the INSERT; not supplied by the API caller.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Persisted as a non-null column in the INSERT statement.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-15 08:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CreatedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who created the earning record, used for audit trail purposes.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Populated from the `UserId` input parameter of the service; not supplied by the API caller as an earning field.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Persisted alongside `CreatedDate` in the INSERT statement.\n\n**Example:** `admin`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "UpdatedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp of the most recent modification to the earning record, maintained automatically by the service layer on every write operation.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Set to `now` on INSERT (same value as `CreatedDate`).\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Set to `now` on every UPDATE operation.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:UpdatedDate, \"UpdatedDate\")`.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-15 08:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "UpdatedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who last modified the earning record, used for audit trail purposes.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Set to `UserId` on INSERT (same value as `CreatedBy`).\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Set to `UserId` on every UPDATE operation.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/earning/UpdateEarning.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:UpdatedBy, \"UpdatedBy\")`.\n\n**Example:** `admin`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "DeletedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp recording when the earning record was soft-deleted; null indicates the record is active.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/DeleteEarning.gloop`]\n- Set to the current server timestamp (`now`) by the service layer when a delete is executed; not supplied by the API caller.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/earning/SelectEarning.gloop`]\n- All SELECT queries filter on `\"Deleted\" = 0`, so soft-deleted records (where `DeletedDate` is non-null) are excluded from all read operations.\n\n**Example:** `null`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "DeletedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who soft-deleted the earning record, used for audit trail purposes.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/DeleteEarning.gloop`]\n- Populated from the `UserId` input parameter at delete time; mapped to `deleteEarningInput.DeletedBy` before the SQL soft-delete UPDATE is executed.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/earning/DeleteEarning.gloop`]\n- Persisted via `COALESCE(:DeletedBy, \"DeletedBy\")` in the soft-delete UPDATE statement.\n\n**Example:** `null`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Deleted" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Soft-delete flag indicating whether this earning record has been logically removed; stored as a boolean (false = active, true = deleted).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/earning/SelectEarning.gloop`]\n- All SELECT queries filter on `\"Deleted\" = 0`; records where `Deleted` is true are invisible to all read operations across the application.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/DeleteEarning.gloop`]\n- Set to true (stored as integer 1) via the soft-delete SQL UPDATE. The same SQL statement also sets `Active = 0` and overwrites `Name`, `Code`, and `Description` with obfuscated placeholder strings. The record is never physically removed.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/earning/InsertEarning.gloop`]\n- Implicitly false (0) on INSERT; no explicit assignment is needed since the database default is 0.\n\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          }
        },
        "additionalProperties" : false
      },
