      "lonti_app_payroll_model_Attendance_Summary" : {
        "properties" : {
          "Id" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Unique auto-generated primary key for the attendance summary record.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/InsertAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- Populated from the database-generated key after a successful INSERT (`$getGeneratedKeys` flag set to true): `$gloopOutput.generatedKeys.Id`.\n- After insertion, checked alongside `attendanceSummaryUpdateCount > 0` to confirm the record was created before logging to the tracker and proceeding with the accrual balance update.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/UpdateAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/DeleteAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- Used as the lookup key in a SELECT-before-mutate check; a null result produces a 404 \"record not found\" response before any DML is executed.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 19, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "EarningCode" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Denormalized short code of the Earning component at the time of import (e.g., \"OT\", \"SL\"), cached on the record to preserve the earning identifier without requiring a join.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/ValidateAttendanceSummaryDetails.gloop`]\n- Sourced from the CSV column `EarningCode`; resolved to a full Earning record via `SelectEarningByCode`. The earning must exist, belong to the same company as the pay period, be assigned to the worker or their position, and have `NeedAttendance = true`.\n- The resolved `Earning.Code` (not the raw CSV value) is mapped onto the attendance summary record: `attendancesummary.EarningCode = earning.Code`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/InsertAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/DeleteAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- Treated as a sensitive field; redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful INSERT or DELETE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/attendance_summary/UpdateAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- Present in the UPDATE SQL via `COALESCE(:EarningCode, \"EarningCode\")`; however, the `UpdateAttendanceSummary` service layer never supplies this field, so it effectively remains immutable after creation.\n\n**Example:** `REG`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 19, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Amount" : {
            "type" : "number",
            "description" : "The monetary or unit amount configured on the Earning at the time the attendance summary was imported; serves as a snapshot of the earning's configured value.\n\nNOTE: This property is not actively used in payroll calculation logic within the attendance summary services themselves. It is persisted as a snapshot for audit and reference purposes.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/ValidateAttendanceSummaryDetails.gloop`]\n- Sourced directly from `Earning.Amount` during validation: `attendancesummary.Amount = earning.Amount`. It is not supplied by the CSV; it is resolved automatically from the linked earning record.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/attendance_summary/UpdateAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- Present in the UPDATE SQL via `COALESCE(:Amount, \"Amount\")`; however, the `UpdateAttendanceSummary` service layer never supplies this field, so it effectively remains immutable after creation.\n\n**Example:** `8.0`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 19, 2026",
            "format" : "double",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "UnitsType" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The unit of measurement for the time or quantity recorded in `UnitsWorked`. Allowed values: `DAY`, `HOUR`, `UNIT`.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/ValidateAttendanceSummaryDetails.gloop`]\n- Sourced from the CSV column `UnitsType`.\n- Validated during import: must be one of `[\"DAY\", \"HOUR\", \"UNIT\"]`; if invalid, the error message `'UnitsType invalid. Valid choices are [DAY, HOUR, UNIT].'` is added and the record is rejected.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/UpdateAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- One of only three fields that may be modified after creation (alongside `UnitsWorked` and `Remarks`).\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:UnitsType, \"UnitsType\")`, so it is only changed when an explicit non-null value is supplied.\n\n**Example:** `HOUR`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 19, 2026",
            "nullable" : true,
            "enum" : [ "DAY", "HOUR", "UNIT" ]
          },
          "UnitsWorked" : {
            "type" : "number",
            "description" : "The quantity of units the worker performed or consumed for this earning within the pay period.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/ValidateAttendanceSummaryDetails.gloop`]\n- Sourced from the CSV column `UnitsWorked`.\n- Validated during import: must be a parseable numeric value (`csvLine.UnitsWorked.isNumber()`); if not, the error `'UnitsWorked not a valid number.'` is added and the record is rejected.\n- Used in accrual balance validation: when `Earning.AccrualId != null` and `allowNegativeBalance = false`, the check `(accrualbalance.Balance - csvLine.UnitsWorked.toDouble()) >= 0` is applied; failure produces `'Worker does not have sufficient credits for Leave.'`.\n- Used to compute the accrual balance update: `Balance = accrualbalance.Balance - UnitsWorked`, `Used = accrualbalance.Used + UnitsWorked`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/UpdateAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- One of only three fields that may be modified after creation (alongside `UnitsType` and `Remarks`).\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:UnitsWorked, \"UnitsWorked\")`, so it is only changed when an explicit non-null value is supplied.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/attendance_summary/SelectAttendanceSummaryCountByPayPeriodWorkerEarning.gloop`]\n- Not used in the uniqueness count query directly, but the combination check `(PayPeriodId, WorkerId, EarningId)` returning a count > 0 prevents re-importing an existing entry.\n\n**Example:** `8.0`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 19, 2026",
            "format" : "double",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Remarks" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Optional free-text notes or context accompanying the attendance entry (e.g., reason for leave, project code, shift description).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/ValidateAttendanceSummaryDetails.gloop`]\n- Sourced from the CSV column `Remarks`.\n- Included as part of the in-memory deduplication key: `FirstName + LastName + EarningCode + UnitsWorked + UnitsType + Remarks`. Two rows are considered duplicates only if all six fields match exactly.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/InsertAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/UpdateAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/DeleteAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- Treated as a sensitive field; redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful INSERT, UPDATE, or DELETE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/UpdateAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- One of only three fields that may be modified after creation (alongside `UnitsWorked` and `UnitsType`).\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:Remarks, \"Remarks\")`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/attendance_summary/DeleteAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- Overwritten during soft-delete with a system-generated label: `'Deleted Attendance Summary {Id} Remarks'`, obscuring the original content.\n\n**Example:** `Regular work hours`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 19, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "EarningId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Foreign key referencing the Earning component this attendance entry is recorded against.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/ValidateAttendanceSummaryDetails.gloop`]\n- Resolved during import by looking up the Earning via `EarningCode`; the resolved `Earning.Id` is mapped onto the record.\n- The earning must satisfy four conditions: (1) exist, (2) belong to the same company as the pay period, (3) be assigned to the worker or their position, and (4) have `NeedAttendance = true`.\n- If the resolved earning has a non-null `AccrualId`, the import also looks up the worker's `AccrualBalance` via `SelectAccrualBalanceByAccrualAndWorker` to prepare the balance update.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/attendance_summary/SelectAttendanceSummaryCountByPayPeriodWorkerEarning.gloop`]\n- Used as one of three keys in the duplicate-check query `(PayPeriodId, WorkerId, EarningId)`; a count > 0 produces the error `'Record already exists.'`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/attendance_summary/UpdateAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- Present in the UPDATE SQL via COALESCE; the service layer never supplies it, so it is effectively immutable after creation.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 19, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "PayPeriodId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Foreign key referencing the PayPeriod this attendance entry belongs to; scopes the record to a specific payroll cycle.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/InsertAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- Sourced from the import input (`attendanceSummaryImport.PayPeriodId`); validated first via `ValidatePayPeriod` before any row-level processing begins.\n- The pay period's `CompanyId` is extracted (falling back to the pay schedule's `CompanyId` if the pay period has no direct company assignment) and used throughout validation to enforce company consistency for both the worker and the earning.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/ValidateAttendanceSummaryDetails.gloop`]\n- Mapped directly onto the attendance summary record: `attendancesummary.PayPeriodId = PayPeriodId`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/attendance_summary/SelectAttendanceSummaryCountByPayPeriodWorkerEarning.gloop`]\n- Used as one of three keys in the duplicate-check query `(PayPeriodId, WorkerId, EarningId)`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/attendance_summary/UpdateAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- Present in the UPDATE SQL via COALESCE; the service layer never supplies it, so it is effectively immutable after creation.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 19, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "WorkerId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Foreign key referencing the Worker who performed or consumed the time recorded in this attendance entry.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/ValidateAttendanceSummaryDetails.gloop`]\n- Not supplied directly in the CSV; resolved during import by looking up the User record via `FirstName + LastName` (`SelectUserByName`), then reading `User.WorkerId`.\n- Two additional checks are applied: (1) the user must have a linked Worker record (`WorkerId != null`), and (2) the worker's `CompanyId` must match the pay period's company.\n- Mapped onto the attendance summary record: `attendancesummary.WorkerId = selectUserByNameOutput.WorkerId`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/attendance_summary/SelectAttendanceSummaryCountByPayPeriodWorkerEarning.gloop`]\n- Used as one of three keys in the duplicate-check query `(PayPeriodId, WorkerId, EarningId)`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/attendance_summary/UpdateAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- Present in the UPDATE SQL via COALESCE; the service layer never supplies it, so it is effectively immutable after creation.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 19, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
