      "lonti_app_payroll_model_Pay_Period" : {
        "properties" : {
          "Id" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Unique auto-generated primary key for the pay period record.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Populated from the database-generated key after a successful INSERT (`$getGeneratedKeys` flag set to true): `$gloopOutput.generatedKeys.Id`.\n- For `SEMIMONTHLY` schedules, two separate INSERT operations run; each produces its own generated Id.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/UpdatePayPeriod.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/DeletePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Used as the lookup key in a SELECT-before-mutate check; a null result from `SelectPayPeriod` produces a 404 \"record not found\" response before any DML is executed.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/ValidatePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Passed as `PayPeriodId` to `SelectPayPeriod`; a null result throws an exception re-raised as 404, blocking any service that requires a valid pay period reference (e.g., `InsertAttendanceSummary`, `ReviewPayrollRun`).\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/DeletePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Used within the soft-delete SQL `CONCAT` expressions to generate placeholder strings for anonymized fields.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "DisplayName" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Human-readable name identifying the pay period (e.g., \"January 2026 - Period 1\", \"Week 3 2026\"). For regular pay periods, this is auto-generated by `PayPeriodCalculator`.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- For regular periods (`OffCycle = false`): auto-generated by `ValidatePayPeriodDetails` via `PayPeriodCalculator`; must be null in the caller's input (validated by `ValidatePayPeriodDetails` — any non-null value returns 400).\n- For off-cycle periods (`OffCycle = true`): required; `ValidatePayPeriodDetails` enforces it is not null.\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful INSERT.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/UpdatePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- One of only four fields that may be modified after creation. Updated via `COALESCE`.\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful UPDATE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/DeletePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful DELETE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/DeletePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Overwritten directly in the database during soft-delete with the placeholder string `'Deleted Pay Period {Id} Display Name'`.\n\n**Example:** `2020-01 Period 1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "StartDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The first day of the pay period. For regular pay periods, this is auto-generated by `PayPeriodCalculator` and cannot be supplied by the caller.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/ValidatePayPeriodDetails.gloop`]\n- For regular periods: must be null in the caller's input; returns 400 if provided. Generated from `PayPeriodCalculator` and returned as `PayPeriodDates.StartDate`.\n- For off-cycle periods: required — `ValidatePayPeriodDetails` enforces it is not null. Validated via `ValidateDates` for format. A date-order check enforces `StartDate <= EndDate <= PayDate`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Immutable after creation; `UpdatePayPeriod` does not accept this field.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-01 00:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "EndDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The last day of the pay period. For regular pay periods, this is auto-generated by `PayPeriodCalculator` and cannot be supplied by the caller.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/ValidatePayPeriodDetails.gloop`]\n- For regular periods: must be null in the caller's input; returns 400 if provided. Generated from `PayPeriodCalculator`.\n- For off-cycle periods: required. Validated via `ValidateDates` and the date-order constraint `StartDate <= EndDate <= PayDate`.\n- Also used in the duplicate-detection query `SelectPayPeriodByPayScheduleStartEndDates` (together with `StartDate` and `PayScheduleId`) to prevent creating an already-existing regular period.\n- Sequential-order check: the new `StartDate` must be after the latest existing period's `EndDate` for the same schedule (`SelectLatestPayPeriodByPaySchedule`).\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Immutable after creation; `UpdatePayPeriod` does not accept this field.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-15 00:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Description" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Optional free-text description of the pay period. For off-cycle pay periods, the service layer appends the working-day configuration to this field on creation.\n\nNOTE: For off-cycle pay periods, `InsertPayPeriod` concatenates the validated `WorkingDays` string to the caller-supplied `Description` (e.g., `\"My bonus period (Working Days included: [MONDAY,TUESDAY,WEDNESDAY,THURSDAY,FRIDAY])\"`).\nThis makes `Description` the only persisted record of which days were counted for the off-cycle period's `WorkDays` calculation. This is a known architectural limitation — a dedicated `WorkingDays` database column is the recommended future improvement.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Optional for both regular and off-cycle periods.\n- For off-cycle periods, the working-day string is appended before INSERT regardless of whether a description was supplied.\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful INSERT.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/UpdatePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- One of only four fields that may be modified after creation. Updated via `COALESCE`.\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful UPDATE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/DeletePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful DELETE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/DeletePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Overwritten directly in the database during soft-delete with the placeholder string `'Deleted Pay Period {Id} Description'`.\n\n**Example:** `First semi-monthly period of January 2020.`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Status" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The current administrative status of the pay period (e.g., `\"OPEN\"`, `\"CLOSED\"`, `\"SUBMITTED\"`), used to track its lifecycle state.\n\nNOTE: This property is currently informational only. No payroll processing logic branches on `Status` to gate operations or filter records — it is stored for administrative tracking and display purposes only.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Optional on creation; passed through to INSERT as-is.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/UpdatePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- One of only four fields that may be modified after creation. Updated via `COALESCE`.\n\n**Example:** `OPEN`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "PayDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The date on which workers are paid for this pay period. For regular pay periods, this is auto-generated by `PayPeriodCalculator`. For off-cycle periods, it must be provided by the caller and must be on or after `EndDate`.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/ValidatePayPeriodDetails.gloop`]\n- For regular periods: must be null in the caller's input; generated from `PayPeriodCalculator`.\n- For off-cycle periods: required. Validated via `ValidateDates` for format. Constraint: `StartDate <= EndDate <= PayDate`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Immutable after creation; `UpdatePayPeriod` does not accept this field.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-20 00:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "SubmitDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The date on which the pay period was submitted for processing or payroll run review.\n\nNOTE: This property is currently informational only. No payroll processing logic consumes `SubmitDate` as a gate or filter — it is stored for administrative tracking purposes only.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Optional on creation; validated for date string format via `ValidateDates` when provided.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/UpdatePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- One of only four fields that may be modified after creation. Validated for date string format via `ValidateDates` when provided. Updated via `COALESCE`.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-18 00:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "WorkDays" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "The number of working days in this pay period. For regular pay periods, computed by `PayPeriodCalculator` based on the pay schedule's working-day configuration. For off-cycle pay periods, computed from the caller-supplied `WorkingDays` string via `PayPeriodCalculator.calculateWorkingDays(StartDate, EndDate, WorkingDays)`.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Not supplied by the caller — always derived from validation/calculation services. Immutable after creation; `UpdatePayPeriod` does not accept this field.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/SelectAllPayComponentByWorkerAndPosition.gloop`]\n- Actively consumed during payroll run assembly for `MONTHLY` and `SEMIMONTHLY` pay schedules to recalculate position rates:\n    - `DailyRate = PayPeriodRate / WorkDays`\n    - `HourlyRate = PayPeriodRate / (WorkDays × (WeeklyHours / WeeklyDays))`\n  This ensures daily and hourly rates correctly reflect the actual number of working days in each variable-length pay period.\n\n**Example:** `11`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "PayScheduleId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Foreign key referencing the `Pay_Schedule` that governs this pay period. Required for regular pay periods; must be null for off-cycle pay periods.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/ValidatePayPeriodDetails.gloop`]\n- For regular periods (`OffCycle = false`): required; validated via `ValidatePaySchedule` to confirm the referenced schedule exists.\n- For off-cycle periods (`OffCycle = true`): must be null; a non-null value returns 400 \"Off-cycle pay periods cannot have an associated 'Pay_Schedule' record.\"\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Immutable after creation; `UpdatePayPeriod` does not accept this field.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/InsertAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- When `PayPeriod.CompanyId` is null, the service falls back to reading `CompanyId` from the associated pay schedule via `SelectPaySchedule` using this `PayScheduleId`.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CompanyId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Optional foreign key scoping the pay period to a specific company. Required for off-cycle pay periods; optional for regular pay periods (which inherit company context from their `Pay_Schedule`).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/ValidatePayPeriodDetails.gloop`]\n- For off-cycle periods: required — `ValidatePayPeriodDetails` enforces it is not null alongside `DisplayName`, `StartDate`, `EndDate`, and `PayDate`.\n- For regular periods: not validated; typically null and derived from the linked `Pay_Schedule` when needed.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Immutable after creation; `UpdatePayPeriod` does not accept this field.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/attendance_summary/InsertAttendanceSummary.gloop`]\n- Extracted from `ValidatePayPeriod` output as the company context for validating worker and earning ownership during attendance CSV import. If `CompanyId` is null on the pay period, it is looked up from the linked pay schedule instead.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "OffCycle" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Boolean flag indicating whether this pay period is off-cycle (ad-hoc) rather than part of a regular pay schedule. Stored as an integer in the database (1 = true, 0 = false). Drives the entire creation validation path and determines which other fields are required or forbidden.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Converted to integer before INSERT: `payperiod.OffCycle == null ? null : (payperiod.OffCycle ? 1 : 0)`.\n- The second pay period inserted for `SEMIMONTHLY` schedules always has `OffCycle = 0` hardcoded.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/ValidatePayPeriodDetails.gloop`]\n- Branched on as the primary gate for the two validation paths:\n    - `true` → off-cycle path: `PayScheduleId` must be null; `DisplayName`, `StartDate`, `EndDate`, `PayDate`, `CompanyId` required; `WorkDays` computed from caller's `WorkingDays` string.\n    - `false` → regular path: `PayScheduleId` required; `DisplayName`, `StartDate`, `EndDate`, `PayDate` must be null; all fields generated by `PayPeriodCalculator`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Immutable after creation; `UpdatePayPeriod` does not accept this field.\n\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "FinalPayEligibleWorker" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Legacy field formerly used to link final-pay-eligible workers to a pay period.\n\n**NOTE:** This property is no longer used by the active final-pay worker retrieval flow. Final-pay worker selection is now driven by `Employment_Info` properties (`FinalPayEligible`, `FinalPayProcessed`, and `TerminationDate` within pay-period range).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Not set on insert for regular periods; only explicitly mapped for the `secondpayperiod` record in semi-monthly insert. Otherwise defaults to null/0 from the database.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ReviewPayrollRun.gloop`]\n- Final-pay worker retrieval calls `lonti_app_payroll.sql.worker.SelectAllFinalPayEligibleWorkerAndPositionByPayPeriod` during termination payroll run handling.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/worker/SelectAllFinalPayEligibleWorkerAndPositionByPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Selection criteria use `EMPLOYMENT_INFO.FinalPayEligible = 1`, `EMPLOYMENT_INFO.FinalPayProcessed = 0`, and pay-period `tsrange(...) @> EMPLOYMENT_INFO.TerminationDate`. `PAY_PERIOD.FinalPayEligibleWorker` is not part of this query logic.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectPayPeriodByWorker.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectAllPayPeriodByWorker.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectAllPayPeriodGroupByWorker.gloop`]\n- Legacy/by-worker pay period selectors still expose this field and join it to `WORKER.Id`, but this path is separate from active final-pay eligibility retrieval.\n\n**Example:** `0`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CreatedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp recording when the pay period record was first inserted into the database.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Set to the current server timestamp (`now`) by the service layer before the INSERT; not supplied by the caller.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-15 08:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CreatedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who created the pay period record, used for audit trail purposes.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Populated from the `UserId` input parameter of the service; not supplied by the caller as a pay period field.\n\n**Example:** `admin`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "UpdatedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp of the most recent modification to the pay period record, maintained automatically by the service layer on every write operation.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Set to `now` on INSERT (same value as `CreatedDate`).\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/UpdatePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Set to `now` on every UPDATE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/UpdatePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:UpdatedDate, \"UpdatedDate\")`.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-15 08:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "UpdatedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who last modified the pay period record, used for audit trail purposes.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Set to `UserId` on INSERT (same value as `CreatedBy`).\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/UpdatePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Set to `UserId` on every UPDATE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/UpdatePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:UpdatedBy, \"UpdatedBy\")`.\n\n**Example:** `admin`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "DeletedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp recording when the pay period record was soft-deleted; null indicates the record is active.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/DeletePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Set to the current server timestamp (`now`) by the service layer when a delete is executed; not supplied by the caller.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectPayPeriod.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectLatestPayPeriodByPaySchedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectPayPeriodByPayScheduleStartEndDates.gloop`]\n- Core lookup queries exclude soft-deleted records with `\"Deleted\" = 0`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectAllPayPeriodByPay_Schedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectAllPayPeriodGroupByPay_Schedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectAllPayPeriodByWorker.gloop`]\n- Several joined/grouped list queries project `Deleted` fields without explicitly filtering `PAY_PERIOD.Deleted = 0`; downstream services must account for this when interpreting results.\n\n**Example:** `null`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "DeletedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who soft-deleted the pay period record, used for audit trail purposes.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/DeletePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Populated from the `UserId` input parameter at delete time.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/DeletePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Persisted via `COALESCE(:DeletedBy, \"DeletedBy\")` in the soft-delete UPDATE statement.\n\n**Example:** `null`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Deleted" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Soft-delete flag indicating whether this pay period record has been logically removed; stored as a boolean (false = active, true = deleted).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectPayPeriod.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectLatestPayPeriodByPaySchedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectPayPeriodByPayScheduleStartEndDates.gloop`]\n- These core lookup queries enforce `\"Deleted\" = 0`, so soft-deleted records are excluded from those paths.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectAllPayPeriodByPay_Schedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectAllPayPeriodGroupByPay_Schedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_period/SelectAllPayPeriodByWorker.gloop`]\n- Some list/grouped queries expose `Deleted` values without explicitly filtering `PAY_PERIOD.Deleted = 0`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/DeletePayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Set to true (stored as integer 1) via the soft-delete SQL UPDATE. The same SQL statement also overwrites `DisplayName` and `Description` with obfuscated placeholder strings. After the pay period is soft-deleted, `DeleteAllPayrollRunByPayPeriod` is called to cascade-soft-delete all associated `Payroll_Run` records. The record is never physically removed.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/InsertPayPeriod.gloop`]\n- Implicitly false (0) on INSERT; no explicit assignment is needed since the database default is 0.\n\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 24, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          }
        },
        "additionalProperties" : false
      },
