            "nullable" : true
          },
          "IsTaxable" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Boolean flag indicating whether the employee-side amount of this benefit is subject to income tax. Stored as an integer in the database (1 = true, 0 = false).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/benefit/InsertBenefit.gloop`]\n- Required on creation; `ValidateRequiredFields` enforces that `IsTaxable` is not null.\n- Converted to integer before INSERT: `benefit.IsTaxable == null ? null : (benefit.IsTaxable ? 1 : 0)`.\n- Acts as the parent dependency in `ValidateDependentAttributes`: when true, `TaxExemptionAmount` is required on insert (see `TaxExemptionAmount` property for detail).\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/benefit/UpdateBenefit.gloop`]\n- Optional on update; converted to integer and updated via `COALESCE`.\n- Validated against both new and existing values via dual-state `ValidateDependentAttributes`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessBenefits.gloop`]\n- For `Action = EARNING, Type = PRETAX` benefits: when `IsTaxable = true`, the amount is split between `GrossTaxable` (amount above `TaxExemptionAmount`) and `GrossNonTaxable` (amount at or below `TaxExemptionAmount`). When `IsTaxable = false`, the full amount goes to `GrossNonTaxable`.\n- For `Action = DEDUCTION` benefits: `IsTaxable` is carried through to `DeductionLogs` for payslip display.\n\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 20, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "TaxExemptionAmount" : {
            "type" : "number",
            "description" : "The portion of the employee-side benefit amount that is exempt from income tax. Required when `IsTaxable = true` on insert; meaningful only in that context.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/benefit/InsertBenefit.gloop`]\n- Required when `IsTaxable = true`: `ValidateDependentAttributes` is invoked with `TaxExemptionAmount` as the sole dependent of `IsTaxable`. Because no `CurrentDependents` are passed (insert mode), the validator applies the insert branch — `NewDependents.any { it.value == null }` throws a 400 error — making `TaxExemptionAmount` strictly required when `IsTaxable = true` on creation.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/benefit/UpdateBenefit.gloop`]\n- Optional on update; updated via `COALESCE`. Validated as part of the `IsTaxable` dependent attribute check using existing stored values for dual-state comparison. Because `CurrentDependents` are populated from the database (update mode), a null new value is allowed when an existing value is already present.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessBenefits.gloop`]\n- For `Action = EARNING, Type = PRETAX, IsTaxable = true` benefits:\n    - If `EmployeeAmount <= TaxExemptionAmount`: the full amount is treated as non-taxable (`GrossNonTaxable`).\n    - If `EmployeeAmount > TaxExemptionAmount`: the excess (`EmployeeAmount - TaxExemptionAmount`) is added to `GrossTaxable` and `NetTaxable`; the exempt portion goes to `GrossNonTaxable`. Both portions are logged to `EarningLogs` with appropriate `IsTaxable` flags.\n\n**Example:** `0.00`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 20, 2026",
