          "DeletedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who soft-deleted the benefit record, used for audit trail purposes.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/benefit/DeleteBenefit.gloop`]\n- Populated from the `UserId` input parameter at delete time; mapped to `deleteBenefitInput.DeletedBy` before the SQL soft-delete UPDATE is executed.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/benefit/DeleteBenefit.gloop`]\n- Persisted via `COALESCE(:DeletedBy, \"DeletedBy\")` in the soft-delete UPDATE statement.\n\n**Example:** `null`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 20, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Deleted" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Soft-delete flag indicating whether this benefit record has been logically removed; stored as a boolean (false = active, true = deleted).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/benefit/SelectBenefit.gloop`]\n- All SELECT queries filter on `\"Deleted\" = 0`; records where `Deleted` is true are invisible to all read operations across the application.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/benefit/DeleteBenefit.gloop`]\n- Set to true (stored as integer 1) via the soft-delete SQL UPDATE. The same SQL statement also sets `Active = 0` and overwrites `Name`, `ProviderName`, `Code`, and `Description` with obfuscated placeholder strings. The record is never physically removed.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/benefit/InsertBenefit.gloop`]\n- Implicitly false (0) on INSERT; no explicit assignment is needed since the database default is 0.\n\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 20, 2026",
