      "lonti_app_payroll_model_Calculation_Method" : {
        "properties" : {
          "Id" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Unique auto-generated primary key for the calculation method record.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/calculation_method/InsertCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- Populated from the database-generated key after a successful INSERT (`$getGeneratedKeys` flag set to true): `$gloopOutput.generatedKeys.Id`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/calculation_method/UpdateCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/calculation_method/DeleteCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- Used as the lookup key in a SELECT-before-mutate check; a null result produces a 404 \"record not found\" response before any DML is executed.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/calculation_method/ValidateCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- Passed as `CalculationMethodId` to `SelectCalculationMethod`; a null result throws an exception that is caught and re-raised as a 404 response, propagating the error back to any calling insert or update service.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessBenefits.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessAccrualBalances.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessTaxes.gloop`]\n- At payroll run time, the Id is used to call `SelectCalculationMethod` to hydrate the `Method`, `CalcExp`, and `CalcExp1` fields before the calculation branch is evaluated.\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 23, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Method" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The identifier string that controls how a pay component amount is calculated at payroll run time. Currently only two values are active in the system: `FLAT` and `PERCENT`.\n\n- **`FLAT`**: The configured amount is used directly as-is. No arithmetic is applied.\n- **`PERCENT`**: The configured amount is treated as a multiplier and is applied to the position's `PayPeriodRate` (or `BaseRate` for shift differentials). Effective amount = `configuredAmount × PayPeriodRate`.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n- Branched on after resolving via `SelectCalculationMethod`. `FLAT` uses the earning amount directly; `PERCENT` multiplies by `PayPeriodRate`. The same logic applies to shift-differential calculation via `SDCalculationMethod.Method`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessBenefits.gloop`]\n- Branched on for both the employee-side (`EmployeeCalculationMethod.Method`) and employer-side (`EmployerCalculationMethod.Method`). `FLAT` uses the amount as-is; `PERCENT` multiplies by position `PayPeriodRate`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessAccrualBalances.gloop`]\n- Branched on for encashment calculations. `FLAT` takes `min(Balance, Earning.Amount)`; `PERCENT` computes `Balance × Earning.Amount`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessTaxes.gloop`]\n- Branched on for both employee and employer tax amounts. `FLAT` uses the configured tax amount directly; `PERCENT` multiplies by the relevant taxable base.\n\nNOTE: `ProcessDeductions.gloop` also branches on `Method` in the same pattern, but it is currently inactive and not called during payroll runs. See the architectural note in the top-level model comment for context.\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 23, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CalcExp" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Primary calculation expression string, reserved for future custom formula evaluation.\n\nNOTE: This field is currently not evaluated, executed, or branched on by any payroll processing logic. All calculation decisions are driven exclusively by `Method`. `CalcExp` is reserved for future custom calculation formula support (e.g., rule-engine integration or event-driven extension).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessBenefits.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessAccrualBalances.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessTaxes.gloop`]\n- Retrieved from the database via `SelectCalculationMethod` and mapped into the active payroll processing service's calculation method sub-model alongside `Method` and `CalcExp1`.\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 23, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CalcExp1" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Secondary calculation expression string, reserved for future custom formula evaluation. Intended to complement `CalcExp` for multi-part calculation expressions.\n\nNOTE: This field is currently not evaluated, executed, or branched on by any payroll processing logic. All calculation decisions are driven exclusively by `Method`. `CalcExp1` is reserved for future custom calculation formula support.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessEarnings.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessBenefits.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessAccrualBalances.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/payroll_run/ProcessTaxes.gloop`]\n- Retrieved from the database via `SelectCalculationMethod` and mapped into the active payroll processing service's calculation method sub-model alongside `Method` and `CalcExp`.\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 23, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Custom" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Boolean flag intended to distinguish system-seeded records (`FLAT`, `PERCENT`) from future user-defined calculation methods. Stored as an integer in the database.\n\nNOTE: This field is currently not consumed or evaluated by any service logic. It is reserved to mark future custom records as distinct from system records, enabling protective logic (e.g., preventing deletion or modification of system records) to be implemented.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/calculation_method/SelectCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- Returned as part of the SELECT output but not mapped to any downstream variable in any service or payroll processing pipeline.\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 23, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CreatedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp recording when the calculation method record was first inserted into the database.\n\nNOTE: For the two system-seeded records (`FLAT`, `PERCENT`), this field is set at database initialization time rather than through the service layer.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/calculation_method/InsertCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- Set to the current server timestamp (`now`) by the service layer before the INSERT; not supplied by the API caller.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/calculation_method/InsertCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- Persisted as a non-null column in the INSERT statement.\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 23, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CreatedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who created the calculation method record, used for audit trail purposes.\n\nNOTE: For the two system-seeded records, this field reflects the database initialization context rather than a service-layer caller.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/calculation_method/InsertCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- Column is present in the INSERT statement; however, the `InsertCalculationMethod` service never maps a `UserId` or `CreatedBy` value to this field — it is always persisted as null through the service layer.\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 23, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "UpdatedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp of the most recent modification to the calculation method record.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/calculation_method/InsertCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- Set to `now` on INSERT (same value as `CreatedDate`).\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/calculation_method/UpdateCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- Set to `now` on every UPDATE operation.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/calculation_method/UpdateCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:UpdatedDate, \"UpdatedDate\")`.\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 23, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "UpdatedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who last modified the calculation method record, used for audit trail purposes.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/calculation_method/InsertCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/calculation_method/UpdateCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- Column is present in both INSERT and UPDATE SQL statements; however, neither `InsertCalculationMethod` nor `UpdateCalculationMethod` service maps a `UserId` value to this field — it is always persisted as null through the service layer.\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 23, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "DeletedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp recording when the calculation method record was soft-deleted. Present in the model and returned by `SelectCalculationMethod`, but not actively set by `DeleteCalculationMethod`.\n\nNOTE: The `Deleted`/`DeletedDate`/`DeletedBy` pattern is present in the schema and model but is inconsistent with the hard-delete implementation used by `DeleteCalculationMethod`. These fields are effectively unused for their intended soft-delete purpose on this entity.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/calculation_method/DeleteCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- The delete operation is a hard `DELETE FROM` statement. `DeletedDate` is NOT set — the row is physically removed and this field is never written by the delete service.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/calculation_method/SelectCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- The SELECT query filters on `\"Deleted\" = 0`, which means any record where `Deleted` is non-zero is excluded. In practice, since deletion is hard, this filter only guards against any manually soft-deleted rows.\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 23, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "DeletedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who soft-deleted the calculation method record. Present in the model and returned by `SelectCalculationMethod`, but not actively set by `DeleteCalculationMethod`.\n\nNOTE: See `DeletedDate` for full context on the inconsistency between the soft-delete fields present in the schema and the hard-delete implementation used for this entity.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/calculation_method/DeleteCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- The delete operation is a hard `DELETE FROM` statement. `DeletedBy` is NOT set — the row is physically removed and this field is never written by the delete service.\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 23, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Deleted" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Soft-delete flag present in the schema and model. Returned by `SelectCalculationMethod` and used as a filter in SELECT queries, but not actively set by `DeleteCalculationMethod`.\n\nNOTE: The presence of `Deleted`, `DeletedDate`, and `DeletedBy` in the schema represents an inconsistency between the model structure and the hard-delete implementation. The `DeleteCalculationMethod` service documentation identifies adding soft delete as a future safety enhancement.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/calculation_method/SelectCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- All SELECT queries filter on `\"Deleted\" = 0`; any record where this flag is set to a non-zero value would be excluded from read operations.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/calculation_method/DeleteCalculationMethod.gloop`]\n- The delete operation is a hard `DELETE FROM` statement. `Deleted` is NOT set to 1 — the row is physically removed from the database. The soft-delete pattern used by most other entities in this system is NOT applied here.\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 23, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          }
        },
        "additionalProperties" : false
      },
