            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Deleted" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Soft-delete flag indicating whether this pay slip record has been logically removed; stored as an integer in the database (0 = active, 1 = deleted).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/config/Setup.gloop`]\n- Declared `NOT NULL DEFAULT 0` in the `PAY_SLIP` DDL; implicitly 0 on INSERT.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_slip/SelectPaySlip.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_slip/SelectAllPaySlipByWorker.gloop`]\n- These core lookup queries enforce `\"Deleted\" = 0`, so soft-deleted records are excluded from those paths.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_slip/SelectAllPaySlip.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_slip/SelectPaySlipByPay_Period.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_slip/SelectAllPaySlipByPay_Period.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_slip/SelectPaySlipByPayroll_Run.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_slip/SelectAllPaySlipGroupByWorker.gloop`]\n- These selectors expose `Deleted` values without explicitly filtering `PAY_SLIP.Deleted = 0`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_slip/DeletePaySlip.gloop`]\n- Set to 1 via the soft-delete SQL UPDATE. The same statement also records `DeletedDate` and `DeletedBy`, and overwrites `WorkerName`, `Department`, `PositionTitle`, and `PayPeriodDisplayName` with obfuscated placeholder strings. Unlike other soft-deletable entities in this package, `PAY_SLIP` has no `Active` column; no active flag is cleared. The record is never physically removed.\n\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
