      "lonti_app_payroll_model_Pay_Schedule" : {
        "properties" : {
          "Id" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Unique auto-generated primary key for the pay schedule record.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Populated from the database-generated key after a successful INSERT (`$getGeneratedKeys` flag set to true): `$gloopOutput.generatedKeys.Id`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/DeletePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Used as the lookup key in a SELECT-before-mutate check via `SelectPaySchedule`; a null result produces a 404 `'PaySchedule' record not found.` response before any DML is executed.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/ValidatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Passed as `PayScheduleId` to `SelectPaySchedule`; a null result throws a 404 exception, blocking any service that requires a valid pay schedule reference (e.g., `InsertPayPeriod`, `InsertPosition`).\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/DeletePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Used within the soft-delete SQL `CONCAT` expressions to generate placeholder strings for anonymized fields.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "DisplayName" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Human-readable name for the pay schedule (e.g., \"Monthly Philippines Schedule\"). Together with `CompanyId`, forms the database-level unique identity for the record.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/config/Setup.gloop`]\n- Declared `NOT NULL` in the `PAY_SCHEDULE` DDL. A `UNIQUE` constraint `PAY_SCHEDULE_unique` covers `(DisplayName, CompanyId)` — duplicate display names within the same company are rejected at the database level; violations are surfaced via `GenerateExceptionResponse`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Passed through from caller input; the DB `NOT NULL` constraint enforces it is non-null at persistence time.\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful INSERT.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful UPDATE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/DeletePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful DELETE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/DeletePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Overwritten directly in the database during soft-delete with the placeholder string `'Deleted Pay Schedule {Id} Display Name'`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:DisplayName, \"DisplayName\")`.\n\n**Example:** `Monthly Philippines Schedule`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Description" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Optional free-text description of the pay schedule.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Optional; passed through to INSERT as-is.\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful INSERT.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful UPDATE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/DeletePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Sensitive field: redacted to `\"Redacted\"` in the tracker audit log entry after a successful DELETE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/DeletePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Overwritten directly in the database during soft-delete with the placeholder string `'Deleted Pay Schedule {Id} Description'`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:Description, \"Description\")`.\n\n**Example:** `Monthly pay schedule for Philippines-based workers`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Active" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Flag indicating whether the pay schedule is currently active. Stored as an integer in the database (1 = active, 0 = inactive); exposed as a boolean in the model.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/config/Setup.gloop`]\n- Declared `NOT NULL` in the `PAY_SCHEDULE` DDL; must be supplied on insert.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Converted to integer before INSERT: `payschedule.Active == null ? null : (payschedule.Active ? 1 : 0)`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/DeletePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Explicitly set to 0 on soft-delete (`\"Active\" = 0`), regardless of its previous value.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:Active, \"Active\")`.\n\n**Example:** `true`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Frequency" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The payroll frequency for this schedule. Drives which frequency-specific configuration fields are required or forbidden and determines the number of annual pay periods.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/config/Setup.gloop`]\n- Declared `NOT NULL` in the `PAY_SCHEDULE` DDL; required on insert.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/ValidatePayScheduleFrequencyFields.gloop`]\n- Governs which frequency-specific fields are required or forbidden:\n    - `WEEKLY` / `BIWEEKLY`: `WeekStartDayName` and `WeekPayDayName` are required; all `Month*` day fields must be null.\n    - `SEMIMONTHLY`: `MonthFirstStartDay`, `MonthSecondStartDay`, `MonthFirstPayDay`, and `MonthSecondPayDay` are required; all `Week*` day fields must be null.\n    - `MONTHLY`: `MonthFirstStartDay` and `MonthFirstPayDay` are required; all `Week*` day fields and `MonthSecondStartDay`/`MonthSecondPayDay` must be null.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/ValidatePayScheduleDetails.gloop`]\n- Drives the calculation of `AnnualPayPeriods` via `CalculateAnnualPayPeriods`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- When the frequency changes between the existing and updated record, all `Position` records linked to this pay schedule are located and their pay rates recalculated.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:Frequency, \"Frequency\")`.\n\n**Example:** `MONTHLY`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true,
            "enum" : [ "WEEKLY", "BIWEEKLY", "SEMIMONTHLY", "MONTHLY" ]
          },
          "AnchorDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Intended anchor date for the pay schedule calendar. Nullable.\n\n**NOTE:** This property is currently informational only. `AnchorDate` is present in the `PAY_SCHEDULE` DDL and is included in the `InsertPaySchedule` and `UpdatePaySchedule` SQL statements, but is never mapped from the service-layer inputs (`InsertPaySchedule.gloop`, `UpdatePaySchedule.gloop` do not assign a value for this field from the caller's input). It is persisted as `null` for all records created through the current service workflow.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Column included in INSERT and UPDATE SQL parameters but never assigned by the service layer. Always stored as null.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-15 00:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "DayStartTime" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The time of day at which a new payroll day begins, in HH:MM format (e.g., `\"00:00\"`). Used by the pay period calculator for day-boundary calculations.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/config/Setup.gloop`]\n- Declared `NOT NULL` in the `PAY_SCHEDULE` DDL; required on insert. The model provides a default value of `\"00:00\"`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/ValidatePayScheduleDetails.gloop`]\n- Validated against the regex `/^([0-1]\\d|2[0-3]):([0-5]\\d)$/` for HH:MM format when provided. An invalid format produces a validation error.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:DayStartTime, \"DayStartTime\")`.\n\n**Example:** `00:00`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true,
            "default" : "00:00"
          },
          "MonthFirstStartDay" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "The day of the month on which the first pay period starts. Required for `SEMIMONTHLY` and `MONTHLY` frequencies; must be absent for `WEEKLY` and `BIWEEKLY`.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/ValidatePayScheduleFrequencyFields.gloop`]\n- Required when `Frequency` is `SEMIMONTHLY` or `MONTHLY`; must be null when `Frequency` is `WEEKLY` or `BIWEEKLY`. Populating this field for the wrong frequency returns a validation error.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:MonthFirstStartDay, \"MonthFirstStartDay\")`.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "MonthSecondStartDay" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "The day of the month on which the second pay period starts. Required only for `SEMIMONTHLY` frequency; must be absent for all other frequencies.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/ValidatePayScheduleFrequencyFields.gloop`]\n- Required when `Frequency` is `SEMIMONTHLY`; must be null for `WEEKLY`, `BIWEEKLY`, and `MONTHLY`. Populating this field for the wrong frequency returns a validation error.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/ValidatePayScheduleDetails.gloop`]\n- Part of the `SEMIMONTHLY` balance check (`PayPeriodValidator.validateSemiMonthlyBalance`) that ensures the interval between first and second start days is within the configured `MaxImbalance` tolerance.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:MonthSecondStartDay, \"MonthSecondStartDay\")`.\n\n**Example:** `16`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "MonthFirstPayDay" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "The day of the month on which payment is made for the first pay period. Required for `SEMIMONTHLY` and `MONTHLY` frequencies; must be absent for `WEEKLY` and `BIWEEKLY`.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/ValidatePayScheduleFrequencyFields.gloop`]\n- Required when `Frequency` is `SEMIMONTHLY` or `MONTHLY`; must be null when `Frequency` is `WEEKLY` or `BIWEEKLY`. Populating this field for the wrong frequency returns a validation error.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:MonthFirstPayDay, \"MonthFirstPayDay\")`.\n\n**Example:** `15`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "MonthSecondPayDay" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "The day of the month on which payment is made for the second pay period. Required only for `SEMIMONTHLY` frequency; must be absent for all other frequencies.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/ValidatePayScheduleFrequencyFields.gloop`]\n- Required when `Frequency` is `SEMIMONTHLY`; must be null for `WEEKLY`, `BIWEEKLY`, and `MONTHLY`. Populating this field for the wrong frequency returns a validation error.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/ValidatePayScheduleDetails.gloop`]\n- Part of the `SEMIMONTHLY` balance check alongside `MonthSecondStartDay`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:MonthSecondPayDay, \"MonthSecondPayDay\")`.\n\n**Example:** `30`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "WeekStartDayName" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The day of the week on which the work week starts. Required for `WEEKLY` and `BIWEEKLY` frequencies; must be absent for `SEMIMONTHLY` and `MONTHLY`.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/ValidatePayScheduleFrequencyFields.gloop`]\n- Required when `Frequency` is `WEEKLY` or `BIWEEKLY`; must be null for `SEMIMONTHLY` and `MONTHLY`. Populating this field for the wrong frequency returns a validation error.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:WeekStartDayName, \"WeekStartDayName\")`.\n\n**Example:** `MONDAY`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true,
            "enum" : [ "MONDAY", "TUESDAY", "WEDNESDAY", "THURSDAY", "FRIDAY", "SATURDAY", "SUNDAY" ]
          },
          "WeekPayDayName" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The day of the week on which workers are paid. Required for `WEEKLY` and `BIWEEKLY` frequencies; must be absent for `SEMIMONTHLY` and `MONTHLY`.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/ValidatePayScheduleFrequencyFields.gloop`]\n- Required when `Frequency` is `WEEKLY` or `BIWEEKLY`; must be null for `SEMIMONTHLY` and `MONTHLY`. Populating this field for the wrong frequency returns a validation error.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:WeekPayDayName, \"WeekPayDayName\")`.\n\n**Example:** `FRIDAY`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true,
            "enum" : [ "MONDAY", "TUESDAY", "WEDNESDAY", "THURSDAY", "FRIDAY", "SATURDAY", "SUNDAY" ]
          },
          "AnnualPayPeriods" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "The number of pay periods in a calendar year for this schedule. Computed by the service layer from `Frequency`; not supplied by the caller.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/ValidatePayScheduleDetails.gloop`]\n- Computed by `CalculateAnnualPayPeriods` based on `Frequency`; the result is returned as `AnnualPayPeriods` and the caller does not supply this value.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Mapped from the `AnnualPayPeriods` output of `ValidatePayScheduleDetails` to the SQL INSERT parameter.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:AnnualPayPeriods, \"AnnualPayPeriods\")`.\n\n**Example:** `12`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "WorkingDays" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "A delimited list of valid working day names for this schedule (e.g., `\"MONDAY,TUESDAY,WEDNESDAY,THURSDAY,FRIDAY\"`). Used by the pay period calculator to determine which calendar days count as working days within a generated period.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/config/Setup.gloop`]\n- Declared `NOT NULL` in the `PAY_SCHEDULE` DDL; required on insert.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/ValidatePayScheduleDetails.gloop`]\n- Validated and sanitized via `PayPeriodValidator.validateWeekDays()`. The cleaned value is returned as `cleanedWorkingDays` and replaces the raw caller input before persistence.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- The cleaned value from `ValidatePayScheduleDetails` is mapped to the SQL INSERT parameter.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:WorkingDays, \"WorkingDays\")`.\n\n**Example:** `MONDAY,TUESDAY,WEDNESDAY,THURSDAY,FRIDAY`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CreateDaysInAdvance" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Intended to configure how many days in advance pay periods should be automatically created for this schedule. Nullable.\n\n**NOTE:** This property is currently informational only. `CreateDaysInAdvance` is present in the `PAY_SCHEDULE` DDL and is included in the `InsertPaySchedule` and `UpdatePaySchedule` SQL statements, but is never mapped from the service-layer inputs. It is persisted as `null` for all records created through the current service workflow. No background scheduler or automated pay period creation logic currently reads this field.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Column included in INSERT and UPDATE SQL parameters but never assigned by the service layer. Always stored as null.\n\n**Example:** `7`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "PaidInArrears" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Boolean flag indicating whether this schedule pays workers in arrears (i.e., workers are paid after the pay period ends rather than during it). Stored as an integer in the database (1 = true, 0 = false).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/config/Setup.gloop`]\n- Declared `NOT NULL` in the `PAY_SCHEDULE` DDL; required on insert.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Converted to integer before INSERT: `payschedule.PaidInArrears == null ? null : (payschedule.PaidInArrears ? 1 : 0)`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:PaidInArrears, \"PaidInArrears\")`.\n\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "PayDateOnBD" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Determines how pay dates are adjusted when they fall on a non-business day: `PREVIOUS` shifts the pay date to the previous business day; `NEXT` shifts it to the next business day.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/config/Setup.gloop`]\n- Declared `NOT NULL` in the `PAY_SCHEDULE` DDL; required on insert.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Passed through from caller input to the SQL INSERT.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:PayDateOnBD, \"PayDateOnBD\")`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_period/CalculatePayPeriodDates.gloop`]\n- Forwarded as input to `PayPeriodCalculator.calculatePayPeriod()` for `SEMIMONTHLY` and `MONTHLY` frequencies to determine the direction of pay date adjustment when a calculated pay date falls on a non-working day. Not forwarded for `WEEKLY` or `BIWEEKLY` frequencies, which resolve the pay date directly from `WeekPayDayName`.\n\n**Example:** `PREVIOUS`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true,
            "enum" : [ "PREVIOUS", "NEXT" ]
          },
          "EffectiveFromDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The date from which this pay schedule is in effect. Validated for date format on both insert and update.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/config/Setup.gloop`]\n- Declared `NOT NULL` in the `PAY_SCHEDULE` DDL; required on insert.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Validated for date string format via `ValidateDates` before persistence.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:EffectiveFromDate, \"EffectiveFromDate\")`.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-15 00:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "EffectiveToDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "The date until which this pay schedule is in effect. Nullable; a null value indicates the schedule is open-ended. Validated for date format on both insert and update.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Validated for date string format alongside `EffectiveFromDate` via `ValidateDates`; null is permitted.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:EffectiveToDate, \"EffectiveToDate\")`.\n\n**Example:** `2099-12-31 00:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CompanyId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Foreign key scoping the pay schedule to a specific company. Required; every pay schedule must belong to a company.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/config/Setup.gloop`]\n- Declared `NOT NULL` in the `PAY_SCHEDULE` DDL. FK: `companyid_pay_schedule_fkey` → `COMPANY(Id)` ON DELETE CASCADE.\n- Part of the `UNIQUE` constraint `PAY_SCHEDULE_unique` on `(DisplayName, CompanyId)`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Passed through from caller input to the SQL INSERT; enforced as non-null at the DB level.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:CompanyId, \"CompanyId\")`.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CurrencyId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Optional foreign key linking the pay schedule to a specific currency. Nullable.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/config/Setup.gloop`]\n- Nullable in the `PAY_SCHEDULE` DDL. FK: `currencyid_pay_schedule_fkey` → `CURRENCY(Id)` ON DELETE CASCADE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Passed through from caller input; not validated at the service layer beyond DB-level FK enforcement.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:CurrencyId, \"CurrencyId\")`.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CountryId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Optional foreign key linking the pay schedule to a specific country for geographic jurisdiction and regulatory compliance. Nullable. When provided on insert or update, `ValidateCountryAndState` is invoked to confirm the country exists.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/config/Setup.gloop`]\n- Nullable in the `PAY_SCHEDULE` DDL. FK: `countryid_pay_schedule_fkey` → `COUNTRY(Id)` ON DELETE CASCADE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- When non-null, `ValidateCountryAndState` is called (together with `StateId`) to confirm the country/state combination is valid before persistence.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:CountryId, \"CountryId\")`.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "StateId" : {
            "type" : "integer",
            "description" : "Optional foreign key linking the pay schedule to a specific state or province within the associated country. Nullable. Validated alongside `CountryId` when `CountryId` is non-null.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/config/Setup.gloop`]\n- Nullable in the `PAY_SCHEDULE` DDL. FK: `stateid_pay_schedule_fkey` → `STATE(Id)` ON DELETE CASCADE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Validated as part of the `ValidateCountryAndState` call when `CountryId` is non-null.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Uses a **direct assignment** (`\"StateId\" = :StateId`) rather than `COALESCE`, which means passing `null` will explicitly set `StateId` to null on update.\n\n**Example:** `1`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "format" : "int32",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CreatedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp recording when the pay schedule record was first inserted into the database.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Set to the current server timestamp (`now`) by the service layer before INSERT; not supplied by the caller.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-15 08:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "CreatedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who created the pay schedule record, used for audit trail purposes.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Populated from the `UserId` input parameter of the service; not supplied by the caller as a pay schedule field.\n\n**Example:** `admin`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "UpdatedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp of the most recent modification to the pay schedule record, maintained automatically by the service layer on every write operation.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Set to `now` on INSERT (same value as `CreatedDate`).\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Set to `now` on every UPDATE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:UpdatedDate, \"UpdatedDate\")`.\n\n**Example:** `2026-01-15 08:00:00.000`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "UpdatedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who last modified the pay schedule record, used for audit trail purposes.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Set to `UserId` on INSERT (same value as `CreatedBy`).\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Set to `UserId` on every UPDATE.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/UpdatePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Updated via `COALESCE(:UpdatedBy, \"UpdatedBy\")`.\n\n**Example:** `admin`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "DeletedDate" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Timestamp recording when the pay schedule record was soft-deleted; null indicates the record is active.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/DeletePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Set to the current server timestamp (`now`) by the service layer when a delete is executed; not supplied by the caller.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectPaySchedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectAllPaySchedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectAllPayScheduleByFrequency.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectPayScheduleByName.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectPayScheduleByPosition.gloop`]\n- Core lookup queries exclude soft-deleted records by filtering `\"Deleted\" = 0`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectAllPayScheduleGroupByCountry.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectAllPayScheduleGroupByCurrency.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectAllPayScheduleGroupByState.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectPayScheduleByCompany.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectAllPayScheduleByCompany.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectAllPayScheduleByState.gloop`]\n- Joined and grouped list queries project `Deleted` fields without explicitly filtering `PAY_SCHEDULE.Deleted = 0`.\n\n**Example:** `null`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "DeletedBy" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Identifier of the user who soft-deleted the pay schedule record, used for audit trail purposes.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/DeletePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Populated from the `UserId` input parameter at delete time.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/DeletePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Persisted via `COALESCE(:DeletedBy, \"DeletedBy\")` in the soft-delete UPDATE statement.\n\n**Example:** `null`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          },
          "Deleted" : {
            "type" : "boolean",
            "description" : "Soft-delete flag indicating whether this pay schedule record has been logically removed; stored as an integer in the database (0 = active, 1 = deleted).\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectPaySchedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectAllPaySchedule.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectAllPayScheduleByFrequency.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectPayScheduleByName.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectPayScheduleByPosition.gloop`]\n- These core lookup queries enforce `\"Deleted\" = 0`, so soft-deleted records are excluded from those paths.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectAllPayScheduleGroupByCountry.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectAllPayScheduleGroupByCurrency.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectAllPayScheduleGroupByState.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectPayScheduleByCompany.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectAllPayScheduleByCompany.gloop`]\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/pay_schedule/SelectAllPayScheduleByState.gloop`]\n- Joined and grouped list queries expose `Deleted` values without explicitly filtering `PAY_SCHEDULE.Deleted = 0`.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/DeletePaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Set to 1 via the soft-delete SQL UPDATE. The same SQL statement also sets `Active = 0` and overwrites `DisplayName` and `Description` with obfuscated placeholder strings. Soft-deletion is guarded: if the schedule has associated pay periods or positions (`SelectPayPeriodAndPositionCountByPaySchedule` returns count > 0), the delete is blocked and a 403 is returned. The record is never physically removed.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/service/pay_schedule/InsertPaySchedule.gloop`]\n- Implicitly 0 on INSERT; no explicit assignment is needed since the database default is 0.\n\n**Example:** `false`\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 25, 2026",
            "nullable" : true
          }
        },
        "additionalProperties" : false
      },
