            "description" : "Timestamp intended to record when this scope was soft-deleted. Present in the DDL and passable on INSERT and UPDATE, but **never set by the `DeleteScope` service**, which performs a hard `DELETE FROM \"SCOPE\"` instead.\n\n**NOTE:** This property is currently informational only. `DeletedDate` is present in the `SCOPE` DDL and is included in both `InsertScope` and `UpdateScope` SQL statements, but is never set through the deletion service workflow. It persists as `null` for all records created and deleted through the current service workflow.\n\nRules derived from codebase references:\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/scope/DeleteScope.gloop`]\n- Performs a hard `DELETE FROM \"SCOPE\"`. `DeletedDate` is not set.\n\n[`lonti_app_payroll/sql/scope/UpdateScope.gloop`]\n- Uses `COALESCE` — `DeletedDate` could be set via an explicit update call.\n\n---\n\n**Author:** SaaS Team  \n**Version:** 1.0  \n**Since:** March 27, 2026",
